  "generated_text": "To find the probability that a randomly selected jelly bean is blue, we need to determine the total number of jelly beans and the number of blue jelly beans.\n\n1. Calculate the total number of jelly beans:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total jelly beans} = \\text{Red} + \\text{Green} + \\text{Yellow} + \\text{Blue} = 5 + 6 + 7 + 8 = 26\n   \\]\n\n2. Identify the number of blue jelly beans:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Blue jelly beans} = 8\n   \\]\n\n3. Calculate the probability of selecting a blue jelly bean:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Probability} = \\frac{\\text{Blue jelly beans}}{\\text{Total jelly beans}} = \\frac{8}{26}\n   \\]\n\n4. Simplify the fraction:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{8}{26} = \\frac{8 \\div 2}{26 \\div 2} = \\frac{4}{13}\n   \\]\n\n5. Therefore, the probability that a randomly selected jelly bean is blue is:\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{\\frac{4}{13}}\n   \\]",
  "grade": {
